House of the Dragon had the most watched  series premiere in the history of HBO  but what does the Game of Thrones cast  think of all the hype no one has more  experience as a Targaryen than Emilia  Clarke who famously played Daenerys in  Game of Thrones Clark hasn't spoken up  in interviews or posted on social media  about season one of House of the Dragon  yet but she did offer her opinion on  photos from the set back in June 2021  calling them surreal she told The  Hollywood Reporter those pictures came  out and I was like whoa whoa I was on my  own last time I didn't know I had Pals I  could have had a bunch of friends to  hang out with but yes it's mildly  surreal to be seeing all of that again  but good luck to them is what I would  say I really mean that considering the  new series focuses so much on the  targaryens it only makes sense that  Clark would have some wisdom to impart  to the house of the Dragon cast as it  turns out she offered some guidance to  Emmy nominee Matt Smith who is taking on  the role of the ambitious and chaotic  Damon Targaryen and it's probably not  the advice you would expect beginning  tonight King's Landing will learn to  fear the color gold  in an interview with film critic Jake  Hamilton in March Smith shared the  advice given to him from the OG Queen of  Dragons get used to the wig I spoke to  kind of Amelia about that years ago  which was like oh you know I have to go  through like an hour and a half every  day of putting the wig on and it's a lot  actor Nikolai coster-waldau became a fan  favorite for his performance as Jaime  Lannister who had a roller coaster of an  arc over eight seasons of Game of  Thrones in an interview with people at  the 2022 Cannes Film Festival in May the  Danish actor opened up about his  thoughts on the impending debut of House  of the Dragon he told people I've seen  the trailer it seems very familiar  Miguel sapochnik who's the showrunner  directed some of the big episodes in  Game of Thrones so I have a feeling it's  going to be quite surreal to watch it  House of the Dragon has an incredible  cast I hope they'll have all the success  Jon Snow actor kit Harrington met his  wife Rose Leslie on the set of Game of  Thrones turning their steamy on-screen  romance into real-life happiness so it  makes sense that Harrington plans on  watching House of the Dragon but says it  may be a little painful to watch in an  interview with Insider in October 2021  Harrington admitted that the prospect of  a new show in the world of Westeros  makes him emotional especially since his  experiences on Game of Thrones are still  so recent he told the outlet I think to  see people get into outfits and costumes  that resemble what we wore for all those  years and it has the same music and  style and tone but not be in it there's  going to be a rawness there Arya Stark  actor Maisie Williams is close friends  with Olivia Cook who plays Alison  Hightower in House of the Dragon she  told Variety in May that she will  definitely be watching the show adding I  want to be as supportive as possible to  Olivia as an actress but also I'm just  really curious I'm kind of looking  forward to watching Game of Thrones even  though it's not Game of Thrones and  experiencing it as a person that's not  on it John Bradley who played Samwell  tarly is also excited for the new series  and being able to enjoy it as a viewer  not an actor Bradley told Yahoo news in  May I'm very very excited to watch it  and not be worried that my scene's next  Peter Dinklage echoed the sentiment to  The Independent in January the Tyrion  Lannister actor told the outlet I am  excited to watch House of the Dragon  purely as a viewer not knowing what will  happen next Gwendolyn Christy who played  Brienne of Tarth was asked by extra in  July about House of the dragon and said  she was eager for fans to see it saying  I think it will be great for people to  see what feels like a continuation of  the Game of Thrones story it was so  beloved and still is now and um I will  never stop loving Brienne of Tarth  [Music]
 

